# Motion

Motion explains a change; it never decorates. Quick, quiet, and always optional.

## Tokens

| Token | Value | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `motion.duration.fast` | {{DURATION_FAST}} | Hover, press, small state changes. |
| `motion.duration.mid` | {{DURATION_MID}} | Menus, tooltips, toggles, tab changes. |
| `motion.duration.slow` | {{DURATION_SLOW}} | Dialogs, sheets and page-level transitions. |
| `motion.easing.out` | `cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1)` | Everything that enters or responds. |

Only these durations and this easing exist; the audit flags any other.

## Rules

- Animate opacity and transform; do not animate layout properties.
- Entrances use `easing.out`; exits are as fast or faster than entrances.
- Hover lift (web) or the pressed state (mobile) only on interactive items.
- Continuous animation is allowed only for skeletons and the in-button spinner.
- **Reduced motion:** when the user asks for less motion, durations become 0 and nothing slides or scales. The generated CSS
  already contains this block; never override it. On iOS and Android read the system setting and swap movement for a fade or nothing.
- Never use motion as the only signal; pair it with a word, icon or state change.

## Platform mapping

Web: the `duration-*` and `ease-*` utilities generated from the tokens. iOS and Android: the generated theme's motion values
(see the platform files linked from [SKILL.md](../SKILL.md)).
